# Lua / COB module style

## Non-negotiables

- One global: `ChurchOfBeef`; local alias always `COB`
- Core stays pure (no frames, addon messages, or slash)
- Multi-return errors — not `error()` for expected failures
- Getters hand out **copies**; never expose live tables to UI/Net

## Namespace bootstrap (every file)

```lua
ChurchOfBeef = ChurchOfBeef or {}
local COB = ChurchOfBeef
```

Attach one public table per module (`COB.Ranks`, `COB.DB`, …). Colon methods (`DB:Init(...)`). Helpers stay `local function` — do not pollute `_G`.

## Naming

- Fields: camelCase (`rankId`, `updatedBy`, `toRankId`)
- Module constants: PascalCase where already used
- Slash: `SLASH_CHURCHOFBEEF1 = "/beef"`; chat prefix `|cffffaa00Church of Beef|r`

## Errors and types

```lua
-- ✅ GOOD
return nil, "invalid rank id"

-- ❌ BAD
error("invalid rank id")
```

Validate with `type(x) == "number"`. Lua treats `0` as truthy — never `and/or`-coalesce values that may be `0`.

## Core purity

- No `CreateFrame`, `SendAddonMessage`, or slash registration in `Core/`
- Time via injectable `now` or `time()` (Common/Clock)
- `ResetForTests` must no-op unless `COB._IN_TEST`

## Common agent mistakes

- Hardcoding titles instead of `COB.Ranks` / `Data/Ranks.lua`
- Using AceAddon / `NewModule` / LibStub for Core (breaks offline tests)
- Exposing live tables from getters
- Calling `ResetForTests` outside `COB._IN_TEST`
